    slug: "high-risk-pregnancy-care", category: "MATERNITY", title: "High-Risk Pregnancy Care and Obstetrician in Moradabad", summary: "Individual monitoring and birth planning for pregnancies needing closer maternal or fetal observation.", readingTime: "9 min read", image: "/images/health-library/high-risk-pregnancy-care.webp", imageAlt: "An obstetrician counselling a couple about high-risk pregnancy care", keywords: ["high risk pregnancy care Moradabad", "obstetrician in Moradabad", "best gynaecologist in Moradabad"], treatingDoctor: gynaecologist,
    intro: "A high-risk pregnancy has a greater chance of complications for the pregnant person, baby or both. The term covers a spectrum and does not mean a poor outcome is inevitable; it means care and monitoring are tailored more closely.",
    sections: [
      { heading: "What high-risk pregnancy care is", paragraphs: ["Care may involve more frequent visits, targeted blood tests and ultrasound, fetal growth or wellbeing monitoring, medication review, and a delivery plan that balances maternal and fetal needs."] },
      { heading: "Who may need closer care", points: ["High blood pressure, diabetes, heart, kidney, thyroid or autoimmune disease", "Previous severe pregnancy complication, repeated loss or preterm birth", "Multiple pregnancy, fetal growth concern or placental problem", "Very young or older maternal age and other individual risk factors"] },
      { heading: "Diagnostic and monitoring process", paragraphs: ["Early booking establishes history, medicines, blood pressure, blood and urine results and gestational age. Later testing depends on risk and may include glucose testing, cervical assessment, serial growth scans, Doppler studies or fetal monitoring."] },
      { heading: "Available care options", paragraphs: ["Plans can include nutrition and activity guidance, medicines shown to be safe in pregnancy, blood-pressure or glucose management, prevention strategies, specialist consultation and timing or mode-of-birth planning. Never stop prescribed medicines without advice."] },
      { heading: "Does laparoscopy have a role?", paragraphs: ["Laparoscopy is not part of routine pregnancy monitoring. If urgent abdominal surgery is required, the approach depends on gestation, diagnosis and maternal condition and should be coordinated by surgical, obstetric and anaesthesia teams."] },
      { heading: "What to expect through pregnancy and recovery", paragraphs: ["Visit frequency may increase and the delivery date may change if risks evolve. After birth, monitoring continues because complications such as hypertension, bleeding or infection can occur postpartum. Long-term follow-up may be advised after diabetes or pre-eclampsia."] },
      { heading: "Risks and limitations", points: ["Monitoring reduces risk but cannot prevent every complication", "Tests can produce uncertain findings that need repeat assessment", "Early delivery may be safer in some situations but creates prematurity risks", "Advanced maternal-fetal or neonatal needs may require referral to a higher-level centre"] },
      { heading: "Hospital facilities", paragraphs: womensFacilities },
    ], faqs: [
      { question: "Does high-risk mean Caesarean delivery?", answer: "No. Many high-risk pregnancies can have vaginal birth; mode of birth depends on the specific maternal, fetal and obstetric situation." },
      { question: "Will I need more scans?", answer: "Possibly. Scan timing and frequency depend on the risk, growth and clinical findings rather than one fixed schedule." },
      { question: "Can I continue regular medicines?", answer: "Some are safe and some need adjustment. Review every prescription, over-the-counter medicine and supplement early; do not stop essential treatment on your own." },
    ], doctorAdvice: ["Seek urgent maternity care for heavy bleeding, leaking fluid, severe abdominal pain, reduced fetal movement, seizures, fainting, chest pain or severe breathing difficulty.", "Call promptly for severe headache, vision changes, face/hand swelling, upper-abdominal pain, fever, persistent vomiting or labour symptoms before term."], sources: [{ title: "ACOG: What to expect in a high-risk pregnancy", url: "https://www.acog.org/womens-health/experts-and-stories/the-latest/so-you-have-a-high-risk-pregnancy-heres-what-to-expect" }, { title: "ACOG: Preeclampsia and high blood pressure", url: "https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/preeclampsia-and-high-blood-pressure-during-pregnancy" }],
